query(D).filter(condition_a, condition_b).all()
query(D).filter(and_(condition_a, condition_b)).all()
they're equal, When you pass multiple conditions to filter, 
SQLAlchemy implicitly combines them using the AND operator.
there also have _or from sqlalchemy import func, and_, or_ 
for Complex Logical Combinations
